1
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,358
This is more than the sound of a tabla.

2
00:00:20,358 --> 00:00:23,931
These hands carry years of practice.

3
00:00:23,931 --> 00:00:26,908
A single stroke sounds simple.

4
00:00:26,908 --> 00:00:30,480
Playing it well is another story.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,962
A puppet string.

6
00:00:35,962 --> 00:00:38,578
Hands working a loom.

7
00:00:38,578 --> 00:00:47,080
Three different arts share a difficult learning challenge: the finer details
of movement.

8
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,704
A teacher can spot a mistake in person.

9
00:00:53,704 --> 00:00:57,232
But what happens during solo practice?

10
00:00:57,232 --> 00:01:00,172
You can replay a video.

11
00:01:00,172 --> 00:01:04,288
Who points out your own timing error?

12
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:21,040
That question led to PARAMPARA: a wearable practice companion, designed to
support exercises taught by a teacher.

13
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,431
This is our proposed design.

14
00:01:25,431 --> 00:01:28,176
Sensors would record movement.

15
00:01:28,176 --> 00:01:32,979
Small vibration motors would give practice cues.

16
00:01:32,979 --> 00:01:37,096
A hub would connect the system.

17
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,484
The screen shows source images of the selected components.

18
00:01:45,484 --> 00:01:49,470
The internal 3D structure comes from our CAD.

19
00:01:49,470 --> 00:01:53,456
The physical sleeve has not been built yet.

20
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:03,799
Imagine a short exercise recorded with the teacher’s permission.

21
00:02:03,799 --> 00:02:06,065
You repeat it.

22
00:02:06,065 --> 00:02:12,864
The system would compare timing and adapt its cues.

23
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:18,222
As practice improves, guidance fades.

24
00:02:18,222 --> 00:02:23,290
Then comes an attempt without cues.

25
00:02:23,290 --> 00:02:27,512
The aim is independent learning.

26
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:32,749
What works so far?

27
00:02:32,749 --> 00:02:39,622
A phone practice demo, scoring code and a circuit simulation.

28
00:02:39,622 --> 00:02:41,684
Software checks passed.

29
00:02:41,684 --> 00:02:45,120
These are not hardware tests.

30
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:55,475
We reproduced a method on public drum data and found useful signals.

31
00:02:55,475 --> 00:03:01,832
This does not establish tabla accuracy or improved learning.

32
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:11,387
Next: build one real sensor-and-motor channel.

33
00:03:11,387 --> 00:03:14,979
Test timing and comfort.

34
00:03:14,979 --> 00:03:21,264
Then study it with teachers and learners.

35
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,948
Tabla comes first.

36
00:03:23,948 --> 00:03:29,792
Puppetry and weaving need their own exercises and validation.

37
00:03:29,792 --> 00:03:33,688
One score cannot define every craft.

38
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:43,057
Teachers’ consent and credit come first.

39
00:03:43,057 --> 00:03:52,523
Our question is simple: can technology make the next practice session a
little better?

40
00:03:52,523 --> 00:03:54,552
This is PARAMPARA.
